      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "One missile is a demonstration. Twenty is a policy. The NASA Workbench is fine for your first body, but filling slots by hand gets old fast, so let a GregTech machine do it: your plain §lHV Assembler§r builds Missile Bodies with no research and no data stick.\n\nThe Assembler takes the same parts as the workbench page: three compressed steel plates, four Tier 1 rocket fins and a Tier 1 rocket engine. In place of the guidance computer it wires in 2 Advanced circuits, and it wants 250 L of lubricant in its fluid slot. A Tier 1 body takes 30 seconds at HV. The Tier 2 body works the same way in an EV Assembler: four compressed titanium plates, Heavy Rocket Fins and Engine, 2 Data circuits, the same lubricant, 45 seconds. Check NEI.\n\nA machine-built body has no guidance steps. To make it land closer, put the body and a better Guidance Computer back in the Assembler: 15 seconds at the body\u0027s voltage, and the same body comes out guided. Build four Tier 1 bodies.\n\n[note]The Tier 1 body needs HV power, so an LV or MV Assembler won\u0027t run it, and a Tier 2 body needs an EV one.[/note]",
